From 356fe89f95dfeb7a7d67fc50baad8bf790bf2652 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Albrecht Lohofener <albrechtloh@gmx.de>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 22:13:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] xpath: include clixon_config.h in clixon_xpath_ctx.c

struct xp_ctx has the member xc_invariant only if XPATH_CURRENT_OPTIMIZE
is defined. The define is in clixon_custom.h, which a source file gets
through clixon_config.h. clixon_xpath_ctx.c did not include
clixon_config.h, so it saw the struct without xc_invariant:
ctx_dup() allocated 48 bytes on 32-bit ARM, while clixon_xpath_eval.c
and clixon_xpath_function.c use 56 bytes and set xc_invariant at offset
48 of contexts that ctx_dup() created. That write is past the end of
the allocation.

On 32-bit little-endian ARM with musl, the write hits the byte that
mallocng checks on free(), and clixon_backend aborts with SIGILL in
ctx_free() while it loads the datastore at startup. On x86-64 the
struct padding hides the overflow, and on big-endian MIPS the zero
high byte of the int lands there, so the corruption goes unnoticed.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 lib/src/clixon_xpath_ctx.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/src/clixon_xpath_ctx.c b/lib/src/clixon_xpath_ctx.c
index f1022e67..d8e7f256 100644
--- a/lib/src/clixon_xpath_ctx.c
+++ b/lib/src/clixon_xpath_ctx.c
@@ -36,6 +36,10 @@
  * Clixon XML XPath 1.0 according to https://www.w3.org/TR/xpath-10
  * This file defines XPath contexts used in traversing the XPath parse tree.
  */
+#ifdef HAVE_CONFIG_H
+#include "clixon_config.h" /* generated by config & autoconf */
+#endif
+
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
